/** The guard predicates of the encounter machine, implemented once by the domain (EncounterGuards). */
@Suppress("TooManyFunctions")
interface EncounterPredicates {
    /**
     * The command carries two identifiers of the patient it affects, as the identity service confirms them for this command: the MRN with a
     * valid check digit, plus the date of birth at its recorded precision or the approximate-DOB flag (SI-01 clause e). A room, bed or
     * location is never accepted as an identifier (SI-01 clause b; CTRL-0001-4), whatever channel the command comes from. The identifiers
     * may be confirmed against the record on screen; no wristband scan is required, so the predicate can always be met for a correctly
     * selected patient, including one registered on an unidentified-patient alias with the approximate-DOB flag (SAC-06). The identity
     * service's answer is read as a fact (another module owns it); an unknown answer fails.
     */
    fun patientIdentityConfirmed(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command carries two identifiers of the swap partner's patient confirmed as in patientIdentityConfirmed. The partner is chosen as
     * a patient, never as "the patient in bed n".
     */
    fun swapPartnerIdentityConfirmed(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command carries a triage record that names the tenant's configured triage scale, a level that is one of that scale's configured
     * levels, a chief complaint (a code or original text, not blank), the triage time and the triaging user (§8.4 "scale, complaint,
     * vitals, time"; R11 §5), and, for each vital sign the tenant's triage form marks as required, either a value with its time or "not
     * obtained" with a reason the user chose (for example too unstable, refused, in arrest; the reason list is governed content [HUMAN]).
     * An empty required vital-sign list is valid configuration. Only an absent scale configuration fails (§9.14: the scale is chosen by the
     * hospital). Synthetic configurations in tests are NOT FOR CLINICAL USE.
     */
    fun triageRecordComplete(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command was issued in a mode in which the offline matrix (data, ADR-012, CTRL-0015-3) allows bed allocation. Bed allocation is
     * allowed only in the on-site-cell mode and never in cell-lost, edge-agent or mobile-offline mode (SI-15 clause b, vendor-locked). A
     * client's mode is its mode at issue, not at processing: a command issued offline and synced later fails, although the server
     * revalidates it online (SI-15 clause f). A channel that runs inside the cell (HL7 inbound, the migration loader, plugins, AI agents
     * acting through the cell's API) is in the on-site-cell mode by construction. Internet or WAN loss alone never changes the mode (SI-15
     * clause h; §16.3 L1), so the predicate does not read WAN state. An unknown mode fails. The same definition is used by the bed machine
     * and implemented once in the adt domain.
     */
    fun onSiteCellConnected(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command's target bed is in the bed machine's reserved state and its reservation names this encounter (§8.4 bed "available →
     * reserved/assigned → occupied"; §9.12 "bed request → assign → ready → arrival"). The bed's state and reservation are facts read from
     * the bed aggregate.
     */
    fun targetBedAssignedToEncounter(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The new location period on the target bed, starting at the command's effective time and open-ended, overlaps no location period of
     * any other encounter on that bed. Periods are half-open [start, end); an open period has no end; periods marked entered-in-error are
     * ignored. Occupancy is read only from the encounters' location histories (R11 §5 key rule), never from a separate table (§8.2 "one
     * authority and an exclusion constraint against double occupancy"; §9.12 acceptance).
     */
    fun targetBedFreeForNewPeriod(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command names a swap partner: an encounter other than this one, in the in-progress state, with no open leave entry, whose only
     * open bed period is on the command's target bed, and that target bed differs from this encounter's current bed. The effective time is
     * later than the start of the partner's open period, and no location period of a third encounter on either bed overlaps the time from
     * the effective time onward. Both open periods close and both swapped periods open at the same instant in one command, so neither bed
     * has two occupants at any instant (§8.4 "Transfer / swap bed"; §8.5 bed swap A17).
     */
    fun bedSwapPairValid(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * Each bed of the swap admits the patient moving into it under the same rule as the bed machine's bedRestrictionsAdmitPatient (gender
     * restriction, isolation capability, IPC cohort declarations), and neither bed's room has an active pressure alarm (as bed
     * noActivePressureAlarm). As there, a known mismatch or unknown isolation data fails (the override path SwapBedsWithOverride applies);
     * an unknown patient sex, a gender rule that does not cover the patient, or an unknown pressure signal does not fail and raises
     * raiseBedRestrictionWarning (§9.12 "gender and isolation constraints", "pressure alarms ... block assignment").
     */
    fun swappedBedsAdmitBothPatients(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The user chose an override reason from the coded list clinical-emergency, ipc-approved-cohort or restriction-data-wrong-or-unknown;
     * it is never defaulted, and the command names each restriction being overridden. SI-15 (onSiteCellConnected) and the exclusion
     * constraint are never overridable.
     */
    fun overrideReasonChosen(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command's effective (clinical) time is later than the start of every open entry of this encounter's location history: its open
     * bed period and, while on leave, its open leave entry. For a back-entry, the effective time is the start of its first paper period.
     * With no open entry the predicate fails. So no period or leave entry ever ends at or before its start, and the history stays in
     * clinical-time order (R11 §5; §8.1 P2). The recorded time plays no part (SI-10). A wrong earlier time is corrected with
     * CorrectLocationTime, never by recording a false later one.
     */
    fun effectiveTimeAfterLocationStart(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The user chose the discharge disposition from the tenant's governed disposition list or, when that list is missing or empty, from the
     * vendor baseline list (home, died, left-without-being-seen, against-medical-advice, transfer-out, admitted-elsewhere; §9.14
     * "discharge, admit, transfer out, AMA, LWBS"; §9.18 "the discharge order with disposition"). It is never defaulted. It is never a
     * money fact. Because a baseline list always exists, the predicate can always be met.
     */
    fun dispositionChosen(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * For a cancelled discharge that restores a bed, the command's target bed is either (a) the bed whose period the discharge closed, now
     * in the bed machine's dirty or cleaning state, with no location period of another encounter on it from the discharge's effective time
     * onward: the patient returns to that bed, the closed period is reopened and a held cleaning job stays held; or (b) another bed whose
     * reservation names this encounter and on which the new period, from the command's effective time and open-ended, overlaps no other
     * encounter's period (as targetBedFreeForNewPeriod). Any other target bed fails.
     */
    fun returnBedAvailable(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The discharge being cancelled was fired from in-progress (the patient was in a bed, not on leave). */
    fun dischargedFromBed(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The discharge being cancelled was fired from on-leave. Mutually exclusive with dischargedFromBed and dischargedBeforeAdmission; an
     * unknown origin makes all three false (the cancellation is refused and HIM corrects the record).
     */
    fun dischargedFromLeave(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The discharge being cancelled was fired from arrived or triaged (a departure before admission). */
    fun dischargedBeforeAdmission(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The encounter holds a triage record that is not entered-in-error. */
    fun triageRecorded(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The exact complement of triageRecorded. */
    fun noTriageRecorded(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * For a cancelled transfer: the bed whose period the encounter's last transfer closed is in the bed machine's dirty or cleaning state,
     * and no location period of another encounter on it starts at or after that transfer's effective time; the patient returns to it and
     * its period is reopened.
     */
    fun previousBedAvailable(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command names one boundary of this encounter's location history (the start or end of a bed period or leave entry) and a new
     * effective time for it. After the change every entry still has start before end, the entries stay in order without gaps or overlaps
     * between consecutive bed periods, the encounter's first period starts no earlier than its arrival, and no changed interval overlaps a
     * location period of another encounter on the same bed (entered-in-error ignored).
     */
    fun correctedTimesConsistent(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command carries one or more paper location periods, each with a bed, a start and, except for the last, an end, each labelled as
     * downtime entry with the reference of its paper source (SI-10 clause c; CTRL-0010-5; SAC-47). Every bounded period has start before
     * end; the periods are consecutive and do not overlap one another; they lie within a downtime spell that the site record holds (cell
     * loss, edge-agent or mobile-offline spell) and end before the command's recorded time; the first starts no earlier than the
     * encounter's arrival. The last period is open-ended (the bed the patient lay in when the paper record ends; a discharge on paper is
     * then entered with Discharge at its paper time).
     */
    fun backEntryPeriodsWellFormed(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * No back-entered period, each checked over its own interval only (bounded ones as [start, end), the last from its start onward),
     * overlaps a location period of another encounter on that bed, other back-entries included (entered-in-error ignored); and the bed of
     * the last period is not reserved for another encounter, blocked or closed now. Forward-allocation checks (reservation, restrictions,
     * pressure alarms) are not applied: those decisions were taken on paper.
     */
    fun backEntryPeriodsFree(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The exact complement of backEntryPeriodsFree. */
    fun backEntryPeriodsConflict(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The user chose the reason for marking the encounter in error from the coded list wrong-patient, duplicate-encounter or
     * registered-in-error; it is never defaulted (§9.12 "cancellations with a reason"; §8.4 "Audited").
     */
    fun errorReasonChosen(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The chosen error reason is wrong-patient: the encounter was recorded on this patient but the care was given to another patient. */
    fun wrongPatientError(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The exact complement of wrongPatientError. */
    fun notWrongPatientError(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The command names the encounter of the patient who actually received the care: a different patient's encounter in arrived or triaged,
     * whose two identifiers are confirmed as in patientIdentityConfirmed, with no open bed period, and on whose behalf every location
     * period of this encounter can be re-created at its original times without overlapping any other encounter's period (entered-in-error
     * ignored, this encounter's own periods excluded).
     */
    fun replacementEncounterReady(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * This command is the second half, in the same transaction, of a wrong-patient CancelAdmission that names this encounter as its
     * replacement: the periods it receives are exactly that encounter's location periods with their original times, and none overlaps
     * another encounter's period (entered-in-error ignored).
     */
    fun handOverPeriodValid(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The encounter's coding is complete (the record module's HIM coding queue holds no open coding task for it) and its charge capture is
     * complete (the journal holds every charge event the encounter's clinical activity owes, bed-days to the discharge time included,
     * written to the outbox). These are the answers of the record module and the journal, read here as facts; an unknown answer fails. The
     * predicate never reads payment or any RCM state: an unpaid balance, an unpaid deposit, or a missing or denied pre-approval never makes
     * it false (SI-12; CTRL-0012-3). It acts only after the clinical discharge, which it never blocks.
     */
    fun codingAndChargingComplete(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /** The user chose or typed a reason for this command; it is never defaulted and never blank (§9.12 "cancellations with a reason"). */
    fun reasonEntered(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean

    /**
     * The user holds the privilege this command requires and the action is audited: the audit event (actor, reason, effective and recorded
     * time) is accepted for writing with the change; an audit that cannot be written fails the predicate (Appendix B.3; §8.4 "Audited";
     * §9.12; CTRL-0010-4). The privilege per command is governed configuration: back-entry and time correction need supervisor rights
     * (§9.12 "back-dated events only with supervisor rights"); cancelling a discharge whose disposition is died needs the separate
     * death-reversal privilege (DN-051 items 8, 16 and 19).
     */
    fun privilegedAndAudited(facts: EncounterFacts): Boolean
}

